  "answer": "I'll treat this as a shopizer bug fix and start by reading the bug-fix playbook so the investigation follows that sequence.The admin mapper stores the special end date in the start-date field, and the price calculator then rejects a window that has both dates. I'll lock that in with a failing test before changing either path.A dated special never reached the storefront because product creation stored the discount end date in the start-date field, and the price calculator also required that start date to be both before and after today before it would apply a window that had both dates. Specials with no dates skipped that path and still worked. `PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper` now writes the end date on the end-date field, and `ProductPriceUtils` treats the special as active when the start is already past and the end is still ahead. Fix Root Causes kept the change on those two faults. Laziness Protocol kept it to those two lines. Prove It Works is the Maven run of `SpecialPriceDateTest`, which failed on the missing end date before the change and passed after it.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=SpecialPriceDateTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"live admin and storefront HTTP APIs\"], \"missing\": [\"a running Shopizer server and an admin API fixture that creates a product and reads it back from the storefront\"]}",
